  "document": "Riccardo Massi\nRiccardo Massi is an Italian operatic tenor who had performed at such Italian theatres as both the Giuseppe Verdi Theatre and La Scala. He became known for his role as Mario Cavaradossi in \"Tosca\" which he performed in autumn of 2011 at the Bavarian State Opera and then performed again at the Berlin Opera Theatre in November of that year. His US debut was in February 2012 as Radames in \"Aida\" at the Metropolitan Opera following by another summer performance that year. In the autumn of 2012 he sang in \"Il trovatore\" staged by the Canadian Opera in Toronto and in February 2013 sang Calaf in \"Turandot\" produced by the Royal Swedish Opera. He also became known for his performance as Don Alvaro in \"La forza del destino\" at the Australian Opera and the same year sang in another \"Aida\" production, this time at the Michigan Opera Theatre. From 2013 to 2014 he performed at the Royal Opera House and as Cavaradossi at the Liceu in Barcelona. Later on, he returned to Royal Swedish Opera where he sang the title role in \"Andrea Chenier\" and then another \"Radames\" at the Houston Grand Opera. At the Opernhaus Zurich, he sang Calaf in December 2015."
